## 1 · Project Overview

Enterprise transport/cab routing dashboard built with **Vite + React + TypeScript + Redux Toolkit + RTK Query**.  
Feature name: **Route Maker** (`src/features/route-maker/`).  
Purpose: Operations team assigns employees to cab routes for login/logout shifts, reorders pickup sequences, and monitors route efficiency in real-time.

---

## 2 · Tech Stack & Conventions

| Concern              | Choice                                                                                               |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Build                | Vite 5                                                                                               |
| UI framework         | React 18, TypeScript strict                                                                          |
| State                | Redux Toolkit + RTK Query                                                                            |
| Styling              | **Inline styles with `T` design-token object** (no Tailwind, no CSS modules)                         |
| Maps                 | `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` — `APIProvider` + `Map` + `useMap()` inside a `MapInner` child component |
| Drag & Drop          | HTML5 `DragEvent` API — `dataTransfer.setData / getData`                                             |
| UI component library | Imported via `useUILibrary()` hook — **NEVER** `import X from 'antd'` directly                       |
| Icons                | Custom SVG components in `icons/RouteMakerIcons.tsx`                                                 |
| API key              | `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY` env var                                                                       |

**Style rule:** All colors, spacing, radii come from the `T` object (`constants/designTokens.ts`). Dynamic route colors come from `routeColor(vehicleId, index)` and the `colorMap: Record<number, string>` that is built once with `buildColorMap()` and passed down as a prop.

