## 7 · Google Maps Integration

**Package:** `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`  
**Pattern:** `APIProvider` at top → `<Map>` renders tile layer → `MapInner` child uses `useMap()` hook (critical: `useMap` only works inside `APIProvider`).

**Known bugs fixed in uploaded code (do NOT revert):**

| #   | Bug                                               | Fix                                                 |
| --- | ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | `onLoad` prop doesn't exist on vis.gl `<Map>`     | Use `useMap()` in `MapInner` child                  |
| 2   | `focusRoute(routeId)` lost routes between renders | `routesSnapshotRef` persists routes                 |
| 3   | Dashboard `ROUTES` shape ≠ `RouteData` shape      | `vehicleRouteAdapter.ts` converts                   |
| 4   | Double marker render with MarkerClusterer         | Set `map: null` before handing to cluster           |
| 5   | `options={{}}` silently ignored                   | Use individual Map props instead                    |
| 6   | `fitBounds` called before map projection ready    | 100 ms debounce in `mapBounds.ts`                   |
| 7   | Random coords in old adapter                      | `vehicleRouteAdapter.ts` uses real Waypoint lat/lng |

**Adapter:** `vehicleRouteAdapter.ts → adaptVehicleRoutes(routes, colorMap): RouteData[]`

- Sorts `Waypoints[]` by `Sequence` for ordered polyline
- Uses `Passenger.Lat / Lng` for stop markers — **no random generation**
- `invalidateAdapterCache(routes)` — call after passenger drag-and-drop to force re-render

**Map style:** `CenterMapPanel.tsx` applies `CLEAN_MAP_STYLE` — mutes POI, transit, business icons so route polylines are visually dominant.  
**Env var:** `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY` — warning banner rendered when missing.

