## Keeping mock data working during dev

`RouteMakerPage.tsx` calls the real API. If you want to keep the mock data for
offline development, add `skipToken` from RTK Query:

```ts
import { skipToken } from "@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react";

const USE_MOCK = import.meta.env.VITE_USE_MOCK === "true";

const { data: apiData } = useGetRouteAnalyticsQuery(
  USE_MOCK ? skipToken : QUERY_ARGS,
);

// then in the useEffect:
useEffect(() => {
  const source = apiData ? adaptApiResponse(apiData) : MOCK_ROUTES;
  const cm = buildColorMap(source);
  setRoutes(source);
  setColorMap(cm);
  setCabGroups(buildCabGroups(source, cm));
}, [apiData]);
```

Set `VITE_USE_MOCK=true` in `.env.local` when working offline.
